# Whether every member of a ball with a one-limb center is negative, and the ball is not empty
# (milestone2.md, "One enclosure interface", the row of certainly_negative()): c + r < 0, decided
# exactly as c < -r. False for the empty set and for the whole line (0 < -inf is false). The
# comparison of Ball<T, 1>::certainly_negative (include/kairn/ball.hpp). Exact.
kernel:        ball_negative_1
input:         stored c
input:         stored r
output:        mask m
requires:      ball c r
ensures:       certain m lt x 0 x=c,r exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the center compared with the negated radius (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeBallPredicates.v ball_negative_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the results are masks, which have no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical ball

nr = neg(r)
m  = lt(c, nr)
